1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,000
Huge cargo ships climb stairs of water, like going over a mountain.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,350
This is the Panama Canal, across the narrow middle of the Americas.

3
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:11,550
In the middle of the canal, there is a man-made lake 26 m higher than the sea.

4
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:16,450
A ship goes into a water room called a lock. The gates close, water fills in, and the ship rises.

5
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:21,500
They do this a few times to reach the lake, then go down on the other side.

6
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:26,050
There are no pumps. Lake water flows down by gravity and lifts the ship.

7
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:30,300
Each ship that passes uses about 200 million liters of fresh water.

8
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:34,600
So in dry years, fewer ships are allowed to pass.
